mm: 1.2
kind: board
name: lcd-linux-aarch64
derives-from: generic-linux-aarch64
platform-provider: mm.mcu platform.linux.lcd.device
platform-provider: mm.display platform.linux.lcd.display
---

# lcd-linux-aarch64

The generic hosted board with its MCU and screen pointed at the emulated
ST7789. Everything else is inherited: the same SDK, the same named device
map, and the same RTC and IMU providers.

Rebinding mm.mcu, not only mm.display, is what makes the window real: the
emulated chip sits behind the same seam the real driver talks to, and the
SDL2 window is owned by that MCU provider. A sketch built for this board
drives the chip through the same seam, so Adafruit's ST7789 library draws in
the window too. Selecting this board is the only way anything in the LCD lane
pays for SDL2.
